# "If the player chooses a permanent spell, the effect will apply to any damage dealt by that spell and any damage dealt by
# the permanent that spell becomes when it resolves" (CR 609.7a). Bot2 casts Viashino Pyromancer; in response Bot1 casts Eye for
# an Eye and chooses the Pyromancer spell on the stack. The Pyromancer resolves and its enters ability deals 2 damage to Bot1:
# that is the next damage from the permanent the chosen spell became, so Bot1 is still dealt it and Eye for an Eye deals 2 to
# the Pyromancer's controller, Bot2. The effect outlives the spell object it was made about.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl x2
Eye for an Eye
Island x25

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby x2
Viashino Pyromancer
Island x25

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Viashino Pyromancer.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Eye for an Eye.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Stack.Viashino Pyromancer)
Bot2.Target(Bot1)
[T2 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 18
Bot2.Life = 18
